<content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<div class="os-raise-graybox os-raise-text-center">
  <para>Product Property for Exponents</para>
<hr/>
  <para>If \(a\) is a real number and \(m\) and \(n\) are integers, then</para>
  <para>\(a^m \cdot a^n=a^{m+n}\) </para>
  <para>To multiply with like bases, add the exponents.</para>
</div><br/>
<para>Complete problems 1 - 6 using the product property for exponents.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(d^2 \cdot d^3\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(d^2 \cdot d^3 = d^{2+3} = d^5\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(c^4 \cdot c^6\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(c^4 \cdot c^6 = c^{4+6} = c^{10}\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(k^3 \cdot k^5\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(k^3 \cdot k^5 = k^{3+5} = k^8\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
      <item> \((-v)^2 \cdot (-v)^1\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\((-v)^2 \cdot (-v)^1 = (-v)^{2+1} = (-v)^3\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
      <item> \((m)^4 \cdot (m)^4\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\((m)^4 \cdot (m)^4 = m^{4+4} = m^8\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
      <item> \((-p)^6 \cdot (-p)^8\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\((-p)^6 \cdot (-p)^8 = (-p)^{6+8} = (-p)^{14}\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><div class="os-raise-graybox">
  <para class="os-raise-text-bold">Product Quotient for Exponents</para>
    <hr/>
  <para>If \(a\) is a real number, \(a\neq0\), and \(m\) and \(n\) are integers, then</para>
  <para>\(\frac{a^m}{a^n}=a^{m-n}\), \(m&gt;n\) and \(\frac{a^m}{a^n}=\frac1{a^{n-m}}\), \(n&gt;m\) </para>
  <para>To divide with like bases, subtract the exponents.</para>
</div>

<br/>
<para>Complete problems 7 - 12 using the quotient property for exponents.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(\frac{y^5}{y^3}\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\frac{y^5}{y^3} = (y)^{5-3} = (7)^2\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(\frac{r^4}{r}\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\frac{r^4}{r} = (r)^{4-1} = (r)^3\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(\frac{q^9}{q^2}\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\frac{q^9}{q^2} = (q)^{9-2} = (q)^7\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(\frac{(-u)^5}{(-u)^2}\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(\frac{(-u)^5}{(-u)^2} = (-u)^{5-2} = (-u)^3\)</para>
    <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(\frac{(j)^6}{(j)^5}\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(\frac{(j)^6}{(j)^5} = (j)^{6-5} = (j)\)</para>
    <br/>
</solution></exercise>  
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="12" type="enumerated">
      <item> \(\frac{(-z)^8}{(-z)^6}\) </item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(\frac{(-z)^8}{(-z)^6} = (-z)^{8-6} = (-z)^{2}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
